cargo-pkgbuild: reviewed Arch packaging starter
==============================================

Run `cargo pkgbuild` from a trusted Rust binary crate or workspace member.
The command creates a NEW PKGBUILD in the current working directory. It will
not overwrite an existing path, including a symbolic link. Preserve or move
your reviewed recipe yourself before regenerating; there is no force switch.

This is a draft generator, not an automatic AUR publisher or package auditor.
Before sourcing or building its output, review the entire recipe and supply:

- authentic upstream source URLs, pinned versions and verified checksums;
- source-directory changes inside each build function;
- native library/runtime dependencies and appropriate feature selections;
- tested architectures, documentation and all required license notices.

Prerelease hyphens become underscores in pkgver. The upstream release/tag may
still contain hyphens: do not blindly use the normalized pkgver in source URLs.
Generated architecture entries are suggestions inherited from upstream, NOT
verified portability claims. Only native x86_64 builds of this downstream
package have been exercised; cross compilation is outside this helper's scope.
Custom target directories or Cargo configuration can require recipe changes.

Manifest text is shell-quoted, author comments stay on one line, and NUL bytes
in shell fields are rejected. Named/multiple binary targets are installed by
their real names; library-only crates and virtual workspace roots are rejected.
Choose a concrete workspace member instead. Metadata inspection is offline and
does not resolve/download dependency graphs or create a Cargo.lock file.

The helper invokes the installed Cargo and respects local Cargo configuration.
These improvements do NOT sandbox Cargo, builds, proc macros or build scripts,
nor do they make arbitrary upstream projects safe. Use reviewed inputs and an
isolated build environment. A disk/write error can leave a partial NEW output
file; existing files are never replaced. Inspect any error before using output.

Upstream: https://github.com/kstep/cargo-pkgbuild
Downstream package contributor: Danny (carrolldant-glitch)
